# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# This repo is developed from Windows, WSL and occasionally both in the same
# session, which is how the working tree ended up with every file reporting a
# filemode change (100755 -> 100644) and how `git diff` filled with "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF" warnings. Pinning eol=lf keeps a checkout byte-identical on
# either side of the WSL boundary, so a diff only ever shows a real edit.
#
# Paired with `git config core.fileMode false`, which suppresses the mode churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary

# Generated. Collapse them in review; they are noise, not authorship.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
